A||||6||GT Bastard||light ticking sound.... ideas?||||11
Z||000000||GT Bastard||11-10-1999||12:20 PM||||Recently, GT started making a light ticking noise that increased with engine speed.  I seem to notice it most when the engine is under load. It doesn't sound at all like a loose rocker(had one before.)  It kinda sounds like when you touch a credit card on a set of moving bicycle spokes.... I mechanic friend of mine said that it sounded like it's just the ignition components, but I'm not sure that I buy it.  I can't figure out where it's coming from either.  any ideas?||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||11-10-1999||01:18 PM||||likely an exhaust leak. could be anywhere but start at the head flanges. Yes, a bad ignition wire could do it to. they sound very similar at times. check both. replace the ingnition wires, dist cap, and rotor, if they even look bad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||11-10-1999||02:19 PM||||I'd have to go with the exhaust leak along with Ogre.  What I'd do is grab a rubber hose that's about a quarter inch in diameter (I just use the one I drain coolant with),   and while holding one end real close to your ear, run the other end along the exhaust "mainfolds", and you should be able to figure out where it's coming from.  If your lucky it'll be on the rear bank(nearest the trunk).||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||11-10-1999||03:12 PM||||Make it three votes for exhaust leak.  My 86 SE made a loud ticking under acceleration - turns out there were only five bolts holding the rear exhaust manifold on.<P>Installation of the sixth bolt and torquing the other five has nearly eliminated the ticking.||||reg||1
Z||000004||sluppy123||11-10-1999||09:09 PM||||I would have to say exhaust leak. I had a ticking noise that would onlt be present when the car was acelerating. I checked the manifold gaskets and they were fine. I gave up looking for it but when I pulled the engine I discovered the front manifold had a large crack on the bottom side near #6 cylinder. When I hit the gas the engine would twist back opening the crack up wider, making the ticking louder.||||reg||4
Z||000005||GT Bastard||11-10-1999||09:39 PM||||Thanks for the advice guys...  I'll look into it some more.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Racer 1||11-11-1999||01:38 AM||||Might be worn brake pads they have metal indicators that rub on the disc when they get low. might be a rod going south? Good Luck<P> <A HREF="http://fierorob.homepage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorob.homepage.com/</A> <BR>||||reg||5
